          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "śravaṇa is built on the root √śru, \"to hear\" (MW), with the action suffix -ana. The root is inherited from Indo-European: MW compares Greek klyō, \"I hear\", and English loud. The same root gives śruti, \"what is heard\", the name for the Veda."
